  "body": "Follows #2918 (merged). Part 3 of #917. Effort: high (worked by the `max` tier at the coordinator's order).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Root `Cargo.toml`: the pins `truck-stepio`, `truck-topology` and `ruststep` are removed. The `[patch.crates-io]` git pin of ruststep (#887) and its rationale text are removed. The truck comment now names the reference kernel and #2922.\n- `crates/kernel/Cargo.toml`: the bench dev-dependencies `truck-stepio`, `truck-meshalgo`, `truck-topology` and `ruststep` are removed. The `truck` feature stays.\n- `Cargo.lock` (written by cargo): the packages `ruststep`, `ruststep-derive`, `truck-stepio`, `Inflector` and `derive-new` are removed. Old duplicate versions that only ruststep needed are removed too: `itertools 0.10.5`, `proc-macro-crate 1.3.1`, `toml_edit 0.19.15`, `toml_datetime 0.6.11`, `winnow 0.5.40`.\n- Kernel STEP bench: the truck side is now a recorded reading (`crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement/rows.rs`). The numbers come from the bench's own printout at `4b694c7c7`, before this change. The live solidcore reading is judged against them with the same rules and tolerances. Every pinned verdict string is the same as before.\n- `step_agreement.rs` (498 lines) is split along its seam: `rows.rs` (316), `verdict.rs` (168), `step_agreement.rs` (249). This meets #2800.\n- `step_util/truck_guard.rs` and `truck_read` in `step_util/mod.rs` are removed.\n- `step_import.rs`: the third column of `KNOWN_STEP_VERDICTS` (truck) stays as a record and is not asserted. The truck-only test `truck_side_refuses_a_runaway_face_and_obeys_its_cancel` is replaced by `step_agreement.rs` `recorded_truck_readings_keep_their_findings`.\n- `mesh_deviation_bench.rs` (release lane): the truck column is removed. It was printed and never asserted. The recorded numbers of `917-kernel-pcurves.md` are for two files that are not rows of this bench.\n- Stale comments: `kernel/src/solidcore_import.rs`, `kernel/tests/heal_import.rs`, `app/tests/import.rs` (#887 test doc), `app/src/geometry/import/step_depth.rs`.\n- License notices (`assets/ui/LICENSES.md`, `site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt`): `truck-stepio` is removed. The notices of the truck crates that stay are kept.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2790-remove-truck-step.md`.\n\n## Scope (the maintainer, 2026-11-20)\n\n- This PR removes `truck-stepio`, `ruststep` and `truck-topology` as dependencies of the workspace.\n- The non-STEP `TruckKernel` stays: `crates/kernel/src/truck_impl.rs`, the `truck` feature, and the tests `agreement.rs`, `blend.rs`, `heal_import.rs`. Its removal is #2922 (Part of #27).\n- Thus the first \"Done means\" item of #917 (\"no `truck-*` package in `Cargo.lock`\") is met for the STEP crates only. Nine `truck-*` packages stay in the lock: `truck-base`, `truck-derivers`, `truck-geometry`, `truck-geotrait`, `truck-meshalgo`, `truck-modeling`, `truck-polymesh`, `truck-shapeops`, `truck-topology`.\n- `truck-topology` stays in the lock as a transitive package of `truck-meshalgo`, `truck-modeling` and `truck-shapeops`. No member names it.\n\n## Remaining truck uses (all non-STEP)\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/truck_impl.rs`: `TruckKernel` (booleans through `truck-shapeops`, measure through `truck-meshalgo` tessellation, solids through `truck-modeling`).\n- `crates/kernel/Cargo.toml`: the optional dependencies `truck-shapeops`, `truck-modeling`, `truck-meshalgo` behind the `truck` feature, and the self dev-dependency that turns the feature on for the tests.\n- Root `Cargo.toml`: the pins `truck-meshalgo` and `truck-polymesh` (no member uses `truck-polymesh` directly).\n- Tests: `crates/kernel/tests/agreement.rs`, `blend.rs` (`truck_offers_no_edge_blend`), `heal_import.rs` (`truck_offers_no_heal`).\n- The recorded truck readings in `step_agreement/rows.rs` and `step_import.rs` are data, not a dependency.\n\n## Readings\n\n```\n$ cargo tree --workspace -i ruststep\nerror: package ID specification `ruststep` did not match any packages\n$ cargo tree --workspace -i truck-stepio\nerror: package ID specification `truck-stepio` did not match any packages\n$ cargo tree --workspace -e normal,dev -i truck-topology\ntruck-topology v0.6.0\n├── truck-meshalgo v0.4.0\n│   ├── camcraft-kernel v0.24.0 (crates/kernel)\n...\n```\n\n`#[test]` count of `camcraft-kernel` (`cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --features truck --tests -- --list` plus `--lib -- --list`): 116 before, 116 after. The only difference: `truck_side_refuses_a_runaway_face_and_obeys_its_cancel` (step_import, 4 -> 3) goes, and `recorded_truck_readings_keep_their_findings` (step_agreement, 22 -> 23) comes.\n\n## Tests run\n\nBefore the merge of main (head `2282ab644`):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel`: all binaries green (lib 8; agreement 2 + 2 ignored; blend 6; corrupt_input 6; heal_import 4; import_corpus 4; machining_mesh 7; machining_mesh_bounds 5; machining_mesh_open 6; machining_mesh_parity 7; machining_mesh_shortfalls 3 + 1 ignored; mesh_deviation_bench 1 ignored; solidcraft_hostile 3; solidcraft_import 7; step_agreement 23; step_closed_form 3; step_curve_guard 4; step_import 3; step_twisted_flank 3). The self dev-dependency turns the `truck` feature on, so this is the build with the feature.\n\nOn the merged tree (head `d36602a0b`, after `git merge origin/main`):\n- `cargo metadata --locked`: ok.\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement --test step_import --test mesh_deviation_bench`: 23 + 3 passed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-geometry` with `step_csys_read`, `step_diag`, `step_metre_unit`, `step_twisted_flank`, `step_units`: 11 + 4 + 1 + 2 + 6 passed.\n- `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-app` with `import`, `import_bytes`, `import_outward`, `import_solidcraft`, each `import_step_*`, `step_budget`, `step_chord_units`, `step_fidelity`, `step_nesting`, `tool_csys`, `tool_import_modes`: 20 binaries, all green. `import` has 26 passed, including `step_file_with_empty_parameter_list_imports` (the #887 fixture).\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nPinning tests: the 21 per-file tests of `step_agreement` (each verdict unchanged against the recorded truck side), `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name`, `recorded_truck_readings_keep_their_findings`, `corrupt_step_files_never_panic_or_hang`, and `step_file_with_empty_parameter_list_imports`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run` lists all 248 steps, because `Cargo.toml` changed. They were not run: no release build was permitted in this run. The coordinator starts an independent batch gate on this head.\n- `mesh_deviation_bench` (release lane, ignored) was compiled but not run.\n- The cancel half of the removed truck test has no equivalent: the reader that it cancelled is gone.\n- A wasm32 build (named in #27) was not checked.\n\n## #909\n\nThis PR meets each \"Done means\" item of #909: no `[patch.crates-io]` entry and no `git+` source for ruststep in `Cargo.lock`, and the #887 fixture still imports (`step_file_with_empty_parameter_list_imports` is green). The route is a removal of ruststep, not a new upstream release.\n\nChangelog: The STEP crates of truck (truck-stepio, ruststep and its git pin) are removed from the build; STEP files read through solidcore only.\n\nRefs #27\nRefs #2922\n\nFixes #2800\nFixes #909\nFixes #2790\nFixes #917\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
